            "is_markdown": false,
            "creator": "takeshi.arabiki",
            "time": "2013-03-23T19:12:11Z",
            "attachment_id": 1420,
            "count": 0,
            "text": "Created attachment 1420\nmake insertSource support S4 methods\n\nThere are three issues on insertSource as below:\n1. `differs` function in `.copyMethods` is wrong\n2. `setMethod` does nothing if `cacheOnAssign(where)` is FALSE\n3. the result of `allMethodTables()` is substituted to `methods` when evaluate `length(methods)` and `length(methods)` can be greater than 0\n\n\nI don't know much about S4, but I think the attached patch is useful to fix these issues.\n\nnote:\n`missing(functions) & missing(methods)` will be always `FALSE` by applying the patch when evaluating `force`, because `missing(methods)` is always `TRUE`.\nI think using both of default argument and `missing` function is very confusing.",
            "bug_id": 15242,
            "creation_time": "2013-03-23T19:12:11Z",
            "is_private": false,
            "id": 87402,
            "tags": []
          },
          {
            "creation_time": "2013-03-24T07:17:42Z",
            "bug_id": 15242,
            "text": "Created attachment 1421\nsupport multiple signatures and methods without setGeneric call\n\nI have modified the patch slightly to support multiple signatures and methods without setGeneric call.",
            "count": 1,
            "tags": [],
            "id": 87403,
            "is_private": false,
            "creator": "takeshi.arabiki",
            "is_markdown": false,
            "attachment_id": 1421,
            "time": "2013-03-24T07:17:42Z"
          },
          {
            "creator": "jaganmn2",
            "is_markdown": true,
            "attachment_id": {},
            "time": "2026-10-28T19:38:41Z",
            "creation_time": "2026-10-28T19:38:41Z",
            "text": "Thanks, by just reading I can confirm all of the problems that you mentioned and a few others.  I guess that `evalSource` and `insertSource` are not widely used nor much tested.  (1) and (3) are easy fixes.  (2) warrants more care as it touches `setMethod`, but, right, as we would be conditioning changes on `!cacheOnAssign(where)` (more or less implying `is(where, \"sourceEnvironment\")`, though we could test that, too), the risk of breaking something does seem low.  I am reviewing your patch.",
            "bug_id": 15242,
            "count": 2,
            "tags": [],
            "id": 103987,
            "is_private": false
          }
        ]
      }
